Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:50:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: SGHD title menu options for STEINS;GATE 0

The S;G0 title screen (Game.exe 0x45c1b0 and the routines it calls) follows
the S;G one (same SW_TITLEMODE modes, press start blink, main list fading and
sliding in, sub lists, decided entry blinking), with differences the data
could not express. New optional fields of the SGHD title menu profile; sg-pc
sets none of them and keeps its behaviour:

- Variant 1 (S;G0): mode 0 blacks out only its first frame; mode 5 shows the
  background and the logo only; the decoration is drawn every frame.
- GuideSprite / GuidePosition optional (S;G0 has no guide strip there).
- MenuEntryFlags: an entry shown only while a flag is set; the entries below a
  hidden one move up, it cannot be chosen, the cursor skips it (S;G0 EXTRA
  before flag 860, 0x45bf90 / 0x45c6aa).
- MenuHitSize: the hit areas are the shown entries at MenuPosition.
- MenuMask: a sprite drawn over the entries while they slide in.
- SubAnimation 1 with SubFadeStartFrames, SubPointer and SubWipe: the pointer
  fades in and moves right over the first frames, then bracket and items fade
  in in place while a strip of the background is redrawn over them from a
  growing left edge (0x45ac90 / 0x45b470 / 0x45ba80).
- FlickerShowChance, FlickerDots (1, 2, 3 or no dots, the last first) and the
  S;G0 decoration alpha: pieces at (256 - menu alpha) / 2, dots at the menu
  alpha (0x45b030).
- Logo: animated frames (one every FrameTicks frames) and a text sprite over
  them, faded out by the menu (0x45be40).

Generic code, used by the sg0-pc profile only (TYN).

Verified on MuMu (Android 15 x86_64 emulator, not a real device): sg0-pc
title with the logo animation, press start, menu without EXTRA (no save yet),
NEW GAME by touch; sg-pc title, press start, menu, LOAD sub list and START as
before. Not changed here, seen on both: a sub list cannot be closed with the
Android back key or a two finger tap.

